---
layout: base.njk
title: "Your Clash Royale, on the record"
description: "Elixir keeps every Clash Royale battle, clan week and river race you play, and reads it back: on your Ladder, inside your clan, in a short weekly email, or to your own AI agent over MCP. Card stats are public."
permalink: /index.html
canonical: /
navActive: home
---
{#- The front door, as the canvas's Site board draws it (2026-09-29):
    what Elixir is for a player, then what each part of it does, Drop
    next door, and what everyone is playing. Below the board, the parts
    the page has always had to carry: the agent transcript (an exchange
    says what the record is FOR), the corpus totals baked from
    /api/public/stats at build, and the gate.

    No number on this page is invented. The tiles describe a part of
    Elixir instead of showing a record, because a visitor here has none
    and the page has nobody's to show; the cards' numbers are the public
    endpoint's, drawn by home-live.js when they arrive and absent when
    they do not. -#}
{%- set t = stats.totals %}
{%- set drop = familyBar.products | selectattr("game") | first %}
<div data-home>
<section class="grid items-center gap-6 pt-6 wide:grid-cols-[minmax(0,7fr)_minmax(0,5fr)] wide:gap-10 wide:pt-10">
  <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col items-start gap-5">
    <span class="chip chip--ok"><span class="chip__dot"></span>recording now</span>
    <h1 class="home-title">Your Clash Royale,<br />on the record.</h1>
    <p class="home-lede">
      Elixir keeps every battle, clan week and river race you play, and
      reads it back: on your Ladder, inside your clan, in a short weekly
      email, or to your own AI.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/console/signin?request">Request access</a>
      <a class="btn btn--lg" href="/cards/">{% icon "layout-grid", 16 %}Browse card stats</a>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote m-0">
      Accounts are granted by hand while the record grows. Card stats are
      public; no account needed.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="home-art">
    <img src="/assets/elixir-logo-288.webp" alt="Elixir: a purple elixir bottle wearing a gold crown" width="288" height="288" />
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="home-caps">
  <div class="home-band__head">
    <h2 class="home-band__title" id="home-caps">What Elixir does for you</h2>
    <span class="home-band__note">one account, every piece</span>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-5 wide:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "chart-line", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Ladder</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">How am I actually doing?</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">Your battles read back by mode, day, deck and card. Trophy Road and war never share a column. A mirror, not a coach.</p>
      <ul class="home-tile__sample" aria-label="The modes Ladder reads">
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="mode-chip__dot mode-chip__dot--ladder"></span>Trophy Road</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="mode-chip__dot mode-chip__dot--ranked"></span>Path of Legends</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="mode-chip__dot mode-chip__dot--war"></span>War</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="mode-chip__dot mode-chip__dot--event"></span>Events</li>
        <li class="home-tile__caption">Season, days played, decks and cards, one mode at a time</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/ladder">Open Ladder ›</a>
    </article>

    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "users", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Clan</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">Run the clan without a spreadsheet</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">Write your rules once. Elixir reads each week against them and hands leaders the calls: promotions, welcomes, departures.</p>
      <ul class="home-tile__sample" aria-label="Two of the calls Clan hands leaders">
        <li class="home-tile__row">{% icon "award", 14 %}<span class="grow">Promote to Elder</span><span class="chip chip--warn">waiting</span></li>
        <li class="home-tile__row">{% icon "user-plus", 14 %}<span class="grow">Welcome a newcomer</span><span class="chip chip--warn">waiting</span></li>
        <li class="home-tile__caption">Nobody below co-leader sees a removal</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/docs/bring-your-clan">Bring your clan ›</a>
    </article>

    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "heart", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Friends</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">How are my friends doing?</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">Follow friends and players you like. Every Wednesday Elixir tells you how each of them did, mode by mode.</p>
      <ul class="home-tile__sample" aria-label="What a friend gets in Wednesday's email">
        <li class="home-tile__row">A card of their own, first</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row">Their battles in each mode, never pooled</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row">The deck they played most</li>
        <li class="home-tile__caption">Wednesday&rsquo;s Your friends this week</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/docs/follow-a-friend">Follow a friend ›</a>
    </article>

    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "mail", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Emails</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">Tell me without me asking</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">One short email for each part of your week, each with its own switch. Milestones arrive within the hour.</p>
      <ul class="home-tile__sample" aria-label="The weekly emails">
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="home-tile__day">Mon</span>Clan report</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="home-tile__day">Tue</span>Your week in the Arena</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="home-tile__day">Wed</span>Your friends this week</li>
        <li class="home-tile__row"><span class="home-tile__day">Fri</span>Card of the Week</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/docs/email">See every email ›</a>
    </article>

    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "bot", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Your AI</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">Ask anything about your game</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">Connect Claude or any MCP client to your whole record. It answers from the numbers and shows its work.</p>
      <div class="home-tile__sample">
        <span class="home-tile__ask">Am I getting better, or just grinding?</span>
        <span class="home-tile__tools">players_summary · battles_performance</span>
      </div>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/docs/quickstart">Connect your agent ›</a>
    </article>

    <article class="home-tile">
      <span class="home-tile__head"><span class="home-tile__icon">{% icon "layout-grid", 18 %}</span><span class="home-tile__product">Cards</span></span>
      <h3 class="home-tile__question">What is everyone playing?</h3>
      <p class="home-tile__text">Public stats for every card: how often it is played and how it does, by mode and by month. No account needed.</p>
      <div class="home-tile__sample" data-home-top3 hidden>
        <ol class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-2 p-0" data-home-top3-list></ol>
        <span class="home-tile__caption" data-home-top3-caption></span>
      </div>
      <a class="home-tile__cta" href="/cards/">Browse cards ›</a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if drop %}
<section class="home-drop" aria-labelledby="home-drop">
  <span class="home-drop__mark">{% icon drop.icon, 44 %}</span>
  <div class="home-drop__body">
    <span class="home-drop__eyebrow">A game, next door</span>
    <h2 class="home-drop__title" id="home-drop">{{ drop.label }}</h2>
    <p class="home-drop__text">Know your elixir costs cold. Ranked games, Practice, badges and seasons, signed in with your Elixir account.</p>
  </div>
  <a class="home-drop__play" href="{{ drop.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ drop.action }}, {{ drop.about }} (opens {{ drop.href | host }} in a new window)">
    {% chromeIcon drop.icon, 20 %}{{ drop.action }}{% chromeIcon "arrow-up-right", 18 %}
  </a>
</section>
{%- endif %}

<section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="home-top" data-home-strip hidden>
  <div class="home-band__head">
    <h2 class="home-band__title home-band__title--plain" id="home-top">Most played in Path of Legends this season</h2>
    <span class="home-band__note" data-home-strip-note></span>
    <a class="text-[14px]" href="/cards/?mode=ranked">All cards ›</a>
  </div>
  <ol class="home-strip" data-home-strip-list></ol>
</section>

<section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="home-ask">
  <div class="grid items-start gap-8 wide:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] wide:gap-10">
    <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col items-start gap-4">
      <h2 class="home-band__title" id="home-ask">Ask in plain language</h2>
      <p class="m-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-body">
        Your agent gets the tools, the entitlements on your account, and
        every answer with its sample size. You ask the way you would ask a
        clanmate; the answer comes from the record, with the numbers
        behind it.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-[14px]">
        <a href="/docs/quickstart">Connect your agent ›</a>
        <a href="/examples/play">Every example, start to finish ›</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0">
      {%- set scripts = transcript %}
      {% include "transcript.njk" %}
      <p class="footnote mx-0.5 mb-0 mt-3">
        A real exchange, recorded on 2026-09-10: each question was put to
        the live door, the tools under the window are the ones that
        answered it, and every number came back from them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="home-band" aria-labelledby="home-corpus">
  <div class="home-band__head">
    <h2 class="home-band__title home-band__title--plain" id="home-corpus">What it is reading</h2>
    <span class="home-band__note">the whole record, at the last deploy</span>
    <a class="text-[14px]" href="/data">The corpus ›</a>
  </div>
  {#- The one place a number is gold on the home page: a brand moment
      on the marketing half, not a reading in the console. Baked at
      deploy from the same stats /data draws. -#}
  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">battles</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.battles | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">{% if t %}since {{ t.oldest_battle | day }}{% else %}recorded{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">players</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.players_recording | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">recorded{% if t %} · {{ t.players | number }} observed{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">clans</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.clans_recording | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">recorded{% if t %} · {{ t.clans | number }} observed{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats__cell">
      <div class="label">war weeks</div>
      <div class="stats__value stats__value--brand">{% if t %}{{ t.war_weeks | number }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="stats__note">recorded races</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The FORM LIVES IN THE APP (2026-09-10), on the sign-in card: signing
    in and asking to are one decision, and this half once had a second
    implementation of the same POST that broke silently. This panel
    posts nothing; it says why the gate exists and links to it. -#}
<section class="panel panel--cta mt-14" id="request" aria-labelledby="home-request">
  <div class="panel__body flex flex-col items-start gap-3 wide:flex-row wide:items-center wide:gap-6">
    <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-auto flex-col gap-1">
      <h2 class="panel-title m-0" id="home-request">Request access</h2>
      <p class="footnote m-0">
        Accounts are granted by hand while the record grows. Tell us who
        you are in the arena; the card stats stay public either way.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/console/signin?request">Request access</a>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<script src="{{ "/assets/transcript.js" | asset }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ "/assets/home-live.js" | asset }}" defer></script>
